# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cocos Creator scene / prefab merge rules
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .scene and .prefab are JSON files that carry two things:
#   1. Human-authored content (properties we care about diffing)
#   2. Cocos-editor-managed node UUIDs (`__id__`, `_id`, and @property fids)
#
# The editor RESHUFFLES UUIDs whenever it saves — even when the visible tree
# hasn't changed — because add/delete cycles at any point in the session
# renumber the intra-file `__id__` sequence. When two branches both have
# reshuffled UUIDs, git's default text merge (ort/recursive) happily auto-
# merges hunks from both sides, splicing together a scene where @property
# fids from branch A point at UUIDs that only exist in branch B → dangling
# references → Cocos silently "heals" on load by picking the nearest
# same-type node with a matching name, resulting in wired-up buttons that
# now trigger random labels ten panels away.
#
# `merge=binary` disables auto-merge for these files. Behavior:
#   - If only one side changed: git uses that side, no conflict.
#   - If both sides changed: MERGE CONFLICT, working-tree file untouched,
#     user resolves by choosing a side (typically `git checkout --theirs
#     assets/scenes/Game.scene` when propagating a scene fix downstream)
#     or by re-editing in Cocos.
#
# Trade-off: cross-branch scene propagation now requires explicit
# resolution. That's the point — every automatic scene merge in the past
# has produced a hidden UUID corruption. Explicit is safer.
*.scene merge=binary
*.prefab merge=binary
